HST Office: Sheets tables behave like the tables of the familiar office suite while typing.

Tables are the database ranges with a table style (Insert ▸ Table, or a table of an .xlsx file).
- Calculated columns: a formula typed into a data cell of a table column whose other data cells
  are empty, or all hold one common formula, is filled into every data row of the column
  (a new formula typed into a calculated column replaces it in the whole column). A column of
  other content keeps it. The state is derived from the cells (every data row holds the same
  formula in relative form), so it needs no storage and survives copy, undo, .ods and .xlsx.
- Auto-expansion: typing into the row directly below a table (without a total row) or the
  column directly right of it grows the table by that row or column. The new cells take the
  formatting of the row above or the column to the left (not merging, autofilter buttons or
  conditional formats), a new row takes the formulas of the calculated columns, a new column
  gets a unique "ColumnN" header unless the header itself was typed. The autofilter buttons
  and range and the structured references (Table1[Price]) follow the new range
  (ScDBDocFunc::ModifyDBData).
- Each of them is its own undo step after the input ("Table AutoExpansion", "Calculated
  Column"), so Ctrl+Z right after it undoes only the growth or the fill and keeps the typed
  content, like "Undo Table AutoExpansion"; .uno:HstTableUndoAutoExpand does that only while
  the growth is the last step (for a later smart tag / contextual Table tab button).
- Data ▸ Table ▸ "Automatically Expand Tables" (.uno:HstTableAutoExpand) and "Fill Formulas in
  Tables" (.uno:HstTableCalculatedColumns) switch them off; officecfg
  Office.Calc/Input/HstTableAutoExpand and HstTableCalculatedColumns, default on.
- .xlsx export writes <calculatedColumnFormula> for calculated columns (their cells keep their
  formulas, so the import needs no change).
- A paste or a fill (Fill Down/Right, the fill handle) that reaches the row below or the column
  right of a table grows it the same way, by every row or column it reaches, again as its own
  undo step after the paste or fill (ScViewFunc::PostPasteFromClip, FillSimple, FillAuto).
Not done on API input, with change tracking on or on a protected sheet.

